{"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Checking-from-a-test","title":"Checking from a test","identifiers":["doc:\/\/TrackingPlanTesting\/documentation\/TrackingPlanTesting\/expectTrackingPlan(_:matches:sourceLocation:)"]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/trackingplantesting"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"role":"collection","modules":[{"name":"TrackingPlanTesting"}],"title":"TrackingPlanTesting","externalID":"TrackingPlanTesting","symbolKind":"module","roleHeading":"Framework"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlanTesting\/documentation\/TrackingPlanTesting","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Fail a Swift Testing test when an app’s events no longer match its committed tracking plan, so every change to an event comes with a change to the plan."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"Overview","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The tracking plan is how the people and services that read an app’s events learn what each event"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"holds, so it is only useful while it matches the events. With this test, a change to an event"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"doesn’t pass the app’s tests until the plan is exported again, and reviewers see the change as a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"JSON diff of the plan. The test’s report also says which changes would break payloads from released"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"app versions or records already stored."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlanTesting\/documentation\/TrackingPlanTesting\/expectTrackingPlan(_:matches:sourceLocation:)"},{"type":"text","text":" checks a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TrackingPlan"},{"type":"text","text":" against the plan"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"committed in a directory, as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TrackingPlan.check(againstDirectory:)"},{"type":"text","text":" does. When they differ, it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"records a Swift Testing issue whose comment is the check’s report, the same text the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"check"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"command prints, and it returns the check either way. A plan that is only out of date fails the test"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"as a breaking one does: in both cases the committed plan isn’t what exporting the events writes."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Add the product to an app’s test target, so the check runs wherever the app’s tests do. It imports","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Swift Testing, so it belongs in test targets only. To run the check from the command line or CI","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"without a test, use the app’s own ","type":"text"},{"code":"TrackingPlanCommand","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" executable from ","type":"text"},{"code":"TrackingPlans","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["import Foundation","import Testing","import TrackingPlanTesting","","@Test func eventsMatchTheTrackingPlan() throws {","    let directory = URL(fileURLWithPath: #filePath)","        .deletingLastPathComponent()","        .appendingPathComponent(\"TrackingPlan\")","    expectTrackingPlan(try AppTrackingPlan.trackingPlan, matches: directory)","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The guide "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/trackingplanworkflow","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"covers exporting the plan this test checks."}]}]}],"sections":[],"references":{"doc://TrackingPlanTesting/documentation/TrackingPlanTesting/expectTrackingPlan(_:matches:sourceLocation:)":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlanTesting\/documentation\/TrackingPlanTesting\/expectTrackingPlan(_:matches:sourceLocation:)","url":"\/documentation\/trackingplantesting\/expecttrackingplan(_:matches:sourcelocation:)","abstract":[{"text":"Records a Swift Testing issue when ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"plan"},{"text":" no longer matches the plan committed in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"directory"},{"text":", its comment the check’s report, as the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"check"},{"text":" command prints it.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"expectTrackingPlan"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:13TrackingPlans0A4PlanV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"TrackingPlan"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"matches"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:20FoundationEssentials3URLV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"URL"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"sourceLocation"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7Testing14SourceLocationV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"SourceLocation"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:13TrackingPlans0A9PlanCheckO","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"TrackingPlanCheck"}],"role":"symbol","title":"expectTrackingPlan(_:matches:sourceLocation:)"},"https://tyler-keith-thompson.github.io/Traffluent/documentation/traffluent/trackingplanworkflow":{"url":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/trackingplanworkflow","title":"Exporting and Checking a Tracking Plan","titleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Exporting and Checking a Tracking Plan"}],"type":"link"